### name: link.chain.source-name-is-not-a-later-binder
--- note
Only the first LINK of a pipeline is named after its source: the left
argument of the second is a pipeline that already joined, so `R` there is
the relation, a list, and `R["rv"]` is E_NO_KEY.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","alias":"r","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"RV":{"column":"rv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "S":{"kind":"relation","from":"s","alias":"s","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"SV":{"column":"sv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "T":{"kind":"relation","from":"t","alias":"t","fields":{"TID":{"column":"tid","type":"NUM"},"TV":{"column":"tv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "U":{"kind":"relation","from":"u","alias":"u","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"UV":{"column":"uv","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK(S, _1["id"] == _2["id"]) .> LINK(T, R["rv"] == T["tid"]) .> MAP(RECORD("v", _["tv"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:48
===

