### name: link.chain.a-name-dropped-earlier-is-promoted-again
--- note
Promotion is decided per pair from its two elements (spec §7.4): the first
joined row has no `id`, so U's `id` is promoted into the second.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","alias":"r","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"RV":{"column":"rv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "S":{"kind":"relation","from":"s","alias":"s","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"SV":{"column":"sv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "T":{"kind":"relation","from":"t","alias":"t","fields":{"TID":{"column":"tid","type":"NUM"},"TV":{"column":"tv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "U":{"kind":"relation","from":"u","alias":"u","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"UV":{"column":"uv","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK(S, X, Y, X["id"] == Y["id"]) .> LINK(U, A, B, A["rv"] == B["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("v", _["id"]))
--- expect
SELECT "u"."id" AS "v" FROM "r" "r" INNER JOIN "s" "s" ON (CAST("r"."id" AS NUMERIC) = CAST("s"."id" AS NUMERIC)) INNER JOIN "u" "u" ON (CAST("r"."rv" AS NUMERIC) = CAST("u"."id" AS NUMERIC))
===

### name: link.chain.right-only-field-after-a-left-join
--- note
An unmatched LINK_LEFT row promotes nothing from the right (spec §7.4), so
the first joined row of an unmatched R has no `sv`; SQL would compare NULL.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","alias":"r","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"RV":{"column":"rv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "S":{"kind":"relation","from":"s","alias":"s","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"SV":{"column":"sv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "T":{"kind":"relation","from":"t","alias":"t","fields":{"TID":{"column":"tid","type":"NUM"},"TV":{"column":"tv","type":"NUM"}}},
 "U":{"kind":"relation","from":"u","alias":"u","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},"UV":{"column":"uv","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK_LEFT(S, X, Y, X["id"] == Y["id"]) .> LINK(T, A, B, A["sv"] == B["tid"]) .> MAP(RECORD("v", _["tv"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:63
===

