### name: link.twice.a-relation-joined-again-under-its-alias
--- note
Review 2026-09-28 SQL-09. Joining CUSTOMERS a second time rendered its alias
`c` twice, which the server rejects as ambiguous; SEL answers, so the
translator refuses and the program runs in memory. The position is the
relation joined again.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"ORDERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"orders","alias":"o","fields":{"ID":{"table":"o","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"CUSTOMER_ID":{"table":"o","column":"customer_id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"o","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"CUSTOMERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"customers","alias":"c","fields":{"ID":{"table":"c","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"c","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"PLAIN":{"kind":"relation","from":"plain","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},
 "V":{"column":"v","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ORDERS .> LINK(CUSTOMERS, O, C, O["customer_id"] == C["id"]) .> LINK(CUSTOMERS, A, B, A["customer_id"] == B["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("n", _["B"]["name"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:70
===

### name: link.twice.a-self-join-under-the-alias
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"ORDERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"orders","alias":"o","fields":{"ID":{"table":"o","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"CUSTOMER_ID":{"table":"o","column":"customer_id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"o","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"CUSTOMERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"customers","alias":"c","fields":{"ID":{"table":"c","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"c","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"PLAIN":{"kind":"relation","from":"plain","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},
 "V":{"column":"v","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ORDERS .> LINK(ORDERS, A, B, A["id"] == B["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("n", _["B"]["name"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:16
===

### name: link.twice.a-self-join-of-an-unaliased-relation
--- note
Unaliased, the joined side takes the right binder as its alias, so the two
occurrences stay apart.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"ORDERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"orders","alias":"o","fields":{"ID":{"table":"o","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"CUSTOMER_ID":{"table":"o","column":"customer_id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"o","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"CUSTOMERS":{"kind":"relation","from":"customers","alias":"c","fields":{"ID":{"table":"c","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"NAME":{"table":"c","column":"name","type":"TEXT"}}},"PLAIN":{"kind":"relation","from":"plain","fields":{"ID":{"column":"id","type":"NUM"},
 "V":{"column":"v","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
PLAIN .> LINK(PLAIN, A, B, A["id"] == B["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("n", _["B"]["v"]))
--- expect
SELECT "B"."v" AS "n" FROM "plain" INNER JOIN "plain" "B" ON (CAST("plain"."id" AS NUMERIC) = CAST("B"."id" AS NUMERIC))
===

### name: link.twice.a-three-argument-self-join-of-an-unaliased-relation
